@startuml
' Transfer21.10: existing HTTP/recovery contract + explicit Owner policy20.10.
title Draft isolation, recovery and accepted-once target confirmation
autonumber
hide footbox
actor User
participant "Page / editor" as Main
control "Session coordinator" as Session
participant "Existing HTTP API" as API
participant "Existing correlated log" as Log
control "HTML / passive SVG" as Views
User -> Main : edit draft B (confirmed A stays)
User -> Main : explicit build with manual gate
Main -> Session : immutable submitted B / live attempt
Session -> API : POST /charts/natal
API -> Log : existing request_id/run_id, component transitions, terminal event
User -> Main : optionally edit C while B is pending
alt committed POST chart_ready
 API --> Session : committed DTO B
 Session -> Session : own live target confirmed once
else already_applied
 API --> Session : status only, no ChartDTO
 Session -> API : GET /charts/current
 API -> Log : separate current request / response / terminal
 API --> Session : actual current view
 Session -> Session : confirm only live target + fresh chart_ready birth=B
else lost response / STATE_COMMIT_FAILED / BUILD_TIMEOUT
 API --> Session : existing uncertain outcome
 ref over Session, API
 Existing recovery policy:
 lost response -> bootstrap/current;
 commit failure -> Retry-After then current;
 timeout -> Retry-After + explicit restart confirmation, bootstrap/current.
 No automatic POST or health polling.
 end ref
 Session -> API : permitted safe read
 API -> Log : current request / response / terminal
 API --> Session : actual current or failed read
 Session -> Session : fresh matched live target may confirm once
else RESULT_SUPERSEDED
 API --> Session : superseded
 Session -> API : GET current
 API --> Session : actual view
 Session -> Session : preserving ordinary current, even if birth=B
else validation / capacity / other existing error
 API --> Session : existing ErrorDTO / Retry-After
 Session -> Main : keep draft/confirmed A; existing permitted next action
end
alt accepted chart_ready
 Session -> Main : actual facts + acceptanceSeq/cause/submitted target
 Main -> Views : same accepted snapshot, apply policy once
 alt live changed-birth target confirmed
  Views -> Views : clear selection; three tables first5 once
 else ordinary current / same birth
  Views -> Views : reconcile present unique selection, preserve disclosures
 end
 alt allowCollapse and current draft=B
  Main -> Main : live focus fallback BEFORE hiding editor
  Main -> Main : collapse fields, recovery remains outside
 else different draft C / no collapse permission
  Main -> Main : keep user-open editor and draft
 end
else confirmed empty / unavailable
 Session -> Views : remove numeric facts/image/selection, keep permitted birth/draft
else failed safe read
 Session -> Main : no new acceptance; keep A/draft, recheck only
end
note over Main, Views
Stale/different/empty/failed GET does not confirm B or consume the live target.
already_applied facts come only from GET, no producer-provenance assertion.
Later ordinary current never repeats reset/collapse or hides a user-opened editor.
Manual retry after successful old/empty check follows existing explicit action/gate.
S1 absent/ambiguous clears only affected selection, source rows survive.
Local SVG failure keeps same accepted HTML and a visible image warning.
end note
@enduml
